DICTIONARY DATA (NOT COVERED BY THE APACHE LICENSE)

The dictionary asset dict_mie_v4.bin in the APK is generated at build time
from third-party data. It is distributed under the licences of that data,
not under the Apache License:

* Chinese sections: derived from libchewing-data, dict/chewing/tsi.csv at
  commit ea74f76dd2548b1d65d0ff70c3ae66057a6ad97d
  (https://github.com/chewing/libchewing-data).
  Copyright (c) 2025 libchewing Core Team.
  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any
  later version (licenses/lgpl-2.1.txt).

* English sections: derived from FrequencyWords, content/2018/en/en_50k.txt
  (https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords), by Hermit Dave, 2016.
  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (licenses/cc-by-sa-4.0.txt,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  The word list was produced from the OpenSubtitles 2018 corpus
  (OPUS, https://opus.nlpl.eu/; P. Lison and J. Tiedemann, 2016;
  www.opensubtitles.org).

Changes made: libmie's tools/gen_dict.py converts both sources into the
MIE4 v4 binary format. Chinese readings are re-encoded as half-keyboard key
sequences with phoneme positions. English words longer than 30 bytes are
dropped, at most 5 words are kept per key sequence, and frequencies are
capped at 65535. The exact sources and the generator are referenced in README.md
("Third-party data"), so the dictionary can be rebuilt or replaced.
